# Code owners — reviewers requested automatically on every pull request.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the BASE branch of a pull request, not from the
# branch being merged. That is what lets one repository have two different
# review circles: this copy lives on `main` and names the mentors, while the
# copy on `release/sprint2` also names the Project A team. Nothing else has to
# be configured for that to work — the file simply differs per branch.
#
# Two things that are easy to get wrong:
#
#   * A listed owner without write access to this repository is skipped
#     SILENTLY. No error, no warning — the review request just never happens.
#     If reviewers are not being requested, check collaborator access first.
#
#   * `*` means these people own every file. It does NOT mean a pull request
#     needs all of their approvals: branch protection's "require review from
#     Code Owners" is satisfied by one approval from anyone listed here.
#
